00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:48,540
Scouts master ship in seven minutes or less.

150
00:06:56,060 --> 00:07:00,460
So what is the Dreaded Troop Program Death Spiral?

151
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,660
I mean, that's kind of a dramatic way of putting it,

152
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:05,820
but I got your attention though, didn't I?

153
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:08,780
Why do some troops get off track

154
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:10,300
and begin to lose scouts

155
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:14,100
and the program just kind of folds in on itself.

156
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,940
I think there's a predictable sequence of events

157
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:20,740
that kind of lead to that spiral down to the crash.

158
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:22,620
I'll begin by saying

159
00:07:22,620 --> 00:07:24,740
I don't think scouts are ever the problem.

160
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:26,140
I think it's the way we work with them

161
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,440
that causes most of the problems.

162
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:31,020
So let's go back to when we signed on as a volunteer

163
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:33,080
and we start working with a scout troop.

164
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:35,220
I know many of you started working with a Cub Scout pack.

165
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:36,700
but let's go back to when you start

166
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,140
working with a scout troop.

167
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:42,099
So you go to training and you work at understanding your role

168
00:07:42,099 --> 00:07:45,620
and you evaluate the current practices of the troop

169
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:48,780
against what you learn and you work at it, you try.

170
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:53,560
Now that's one way to approach your role

171
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:55,099
as a scouting volunteer.

172
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:57,219
Another way is not getting trained

173
00:07:57,219 --> 00:07:58,940
and not really learning about your role

174
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:01,860
and just kind of adopting whatever practices

175
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,060
that were present when you signed on.

176
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:07,140
And then a third way is to assume

177
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:09,219
that we already know everything

178
00:08:09,219 --> 00:08:12,099
and we carry on regardless.

179
00:08:12,099 --> 00:08:13,900
or we're working with people who assert

180
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:18,900
that they know everything and we follow them.

181
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,900
Either way we resist examining

182
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:24,740
or improving on what we're doing.

183
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:27,580
So, once again, you can get trained

184
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:29,260
and try and really work at this

185
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:31,820
and try and understand things.

186
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:34,020
or you can not get trained

187
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:35,900
and not bother to learn anything

188
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:38,860
and just kind of follow along with whatever's happening

189
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:41,059
in the troop that you're serving in,

190
00:08:41,059 --> 00:08:43,419
or you can just assume that you know everything

191
00:08:43,419 --> 00:08:46,660
and carry on and work with people

192
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:48,660
who assume they know everything.

193
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:50,620
What I would like us all to do

194
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:53,780
is to examine what we're up to

195
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,220
and improve on what we're doing.

196
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:57,980
Now, nearly every scouting volunteer

197
00:08:57,980 --> 00:09:00,380
is going to hear something about

198
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,340
the mysterious patrol method

199
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:04,660
or the virtues of a boy led troop

200
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:06,420
and they may commit themselves

201
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,900
to understanding and applying the patrol method.

202
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:11,219
Now this is a really crucial juncture here,

203
00:09:11,219 --> 00:09:14,579
because Baden Powell said that the patrol method

204
00:09:14,579 --> 00:09:15,780
or the patrol system-

205
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:18,660
those terms are pretty much interchangeable-

206
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:21,380
was the one essential element of scouting.

207
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,020
and it's not easy to understand

208
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:25,620
because really you really don't see

209
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:28,900
the patrol method applied in youth groups

210
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,459
outside of scouting.

211
00:09:30,459 --> 00:09:32,819
So it takes some time to understand.

212
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:34,780
So you hear about it,

213
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:37,060
you commit yourselves to applying the patrol method

214
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:38,780
and then they apply the concepts

215
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,220
in the practice of the patrol method

216
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:43,140
and the first results are almost always disappointing.

217
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:48,020
From the adult perspective they're pretty disappointing.

218
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:52,260
The scouts they're pretty happy with things.

219
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:54,100
but from the adult perspective,

220
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,540
when you look at the way this works,

221
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:58,580
when you have put everything

222
00:09:58,580 --> 00:09:59,820
in the hands of the scouts

223
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:03,140
and you're working on getting them to be responsible

224
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:05,340
for doing their own thing,

225
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:07,740
they're gonna look kind of incapable

226
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:09,660
or competent or lazy.

227
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:11,500
They're gonna look too young-

228
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:15,260
and we've got to accept the fact that they are young

229
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:17,500
and their efforts are gonna be kind of disjointed

230
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:19,900
and chaotic and they're gonna fall far short

231
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:23,220
of creating that orderliness and efficiency

232
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:27,060
that adults imagined we would create, right.

233
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:30,260
So we know that youth leadership

234
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:33,740
is not going to be a smooth, orderly, efficient affair

235
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:36,820
most of the time and we look at that

236
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:40,140
and we don't see the chaotic kind of uncertainties

237
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:43,740
as a positive indication of growing and developing leaders.

238
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:46,180
Now we look at it and we're kind of disappointed

239
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:48,900
and it's a little scary, you know,

240
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:51,620
And it just it seems purposeless. sometimes

241
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:52,820
We look at that and we say,

242
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:54,940
well, this whole patrol method thing,

243
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:56,300
this whole boy led thing,

244
00:10:56,300 --> 00:11:00,660
I think it's a great idea, but really, you know,

245
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:03,540
we've got to do a lot more supervising here.

246
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:06,060
Once we're not too sure about this whole patrol method thing

247
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:08,240
and we start to interfere a little bit,

248
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,940
we start to run things,

249
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:13,500
we try and make things more efficient and orderly,

250
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:16,060
As we do. that you know, the more we do,

251
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:18,860
the better. the more efficient things are

252
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:20,420
and the more orderly they are

253
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:24,180
and there's less trouble and uncertainty and chaos,

254
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:25,380
The Scouts are gonna be happy

255
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:27,740
to have those things taken care of for them.

256
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:30,420
They won't complain,

257
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:33,820
They'll have fun and they won't have to do a whole lot.

258
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:36,740
Boys like that kind of thing for a little while,

259
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,780
but eventually they're gonna get bored.

260
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:41,580
and then the next step in the spiral

261
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:44,860
is the adults have to start coming up with more new

262
00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:47,580
and even more entertaining experiences,

263
00:11:47,580 --> 00:11:50,540
because Scouts are gonna leave if they don't,

264
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,180
and so they work at this.

265
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:54,780
and then the adults tend to get a little upset

266
00:11:54,819 --> 00:11:57,180
when the Scouts don't properly appreciate

267
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:58,900
all that's being done for them

268
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:01,020
and this turns to frustration

269
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:03,860
and that frustration can harden into resentment

270
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:05,100
and that kind of resentment

271
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:07,180
can lead to all kinds of negative things.

272
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,300
You can have a bad attitude about Scouts.

273
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:11,980
You can start making a lot of rules

274
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:13,459
because you're gonna coerce them

275
00:12:13,459 --> 00:12:16,100
into properly appreciating all the wonderful things

276
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:16,939
that you're doing for them.

277
00:12:16,939 --> 00:12:18,339
You know what I'm saying?

278
00:12:18,339 --> 00:12:19,620
It's that step,

279
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:23,180
That's just one of the twists of the spiral,

280
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:25,860
and that kind of attitude drives a lot of Scouts away.

281
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:28,220
and then, when Scouts start to leave,

282
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:31,380
adults become even more upset and resentful.

283
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:33,140
and adults are already fatigued

284
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:34,540
from trying to hold things together

285
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:35,700
and doing everything.

286
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:37,300
their energy starts to wane

287
00:12:37,300 --> 00:12:39,340
and things kind of spiral down.

288
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:41,460
So how do we avoid this?

289
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:43,940
Well, we need to get trained.

290
00:12:43,940 --> 00:12:45,340
but getting trained is not enough.

291
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:47,540
We can't just passively receive these ideas.

292
00:12:47,540 --> 00:12:48,620
We have to test them,

293
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:50,260
We have to pick them apart,

294
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:51,980
We have to learn about them.

295
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:53,300
and I'll tell you the truth-

296
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:54,900
and a lot of people agree-

297
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:57,820
that our present training doesn't do a very good job

298
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,460
of getting the patrol method across.

299
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:01,460
So you've gotta go a little bit over and above

300
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:02,420
and you've gotta read about it,

301
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:03,260
You gotta think about it,

302
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:04,860
You gotta test it.

303
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:06,700
Then you have to apply the concepts

304
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:07,820
and observe the results

305
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:10,140
and assess the understanding and then try again.

306
00:13:10,140 --> 00:13:11,900
And you need to do this with a group of adults

307
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,900
who are committed to making that kind of thing happen.

308
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:17,620
And then you need to stick with the process

309
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:19,660
and work to understand it

310
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:22,260
and you'll avoid that downward spiral.

311
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:24,780
You come into your role as a volunteer,

312
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:25,980
you get started,

313
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:30,740
you try out this youth led patrol method kind of stuff.

314
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:32,420
It looks chaotic and messy

315
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:34,980
and you begin to slowly take over

316
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,860
and then the scouts

317
00:13:36,860 --> 00:13:37,980
they're happy for a while.

318
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:40,339
then they get bored with what you're doing.

319
00:13:40,339 --> 00:13:41,459
So you try and amp it up

320
00:13:41,459 --> 00:13:43,540
and you try and do more interesting things

321
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:45,339
and that takes a lot of energy.

322
00:13:45,339 --> 00:13:46,980
and then you get a little resentful

323
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:49,260
when they don't properly appreciate all the energy

324
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:50,340
that you're putting into it.

325
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:52,060
Maybe you start making rules

326
00:13:52,060 --> 00:13:54,140
and then the scouts

327
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,740
they don't really care for all that

328
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:57,300
and they're going to start to leave.

329
00:13:57,300 --> 00:13:58,660
and once the first couple do,

330
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,780
you grow resentful about that

331
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:02,980
and the scouts pick up that attitude

332
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:04,220
and pretty soon

333
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:06,220
you've got nothing to work with.

334
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,740
So getting off on the right foot

335
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:08,980
is going to be important.

336
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:12,060
Learning what your role is

337
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:13,860
as a scout leader is going to be important,

338
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:15,660
and really dedicating the time to it

339
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:16,860
and working with it

340
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,860
and understanding that it takes time

341
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:19,700
and patience.

342
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:21,820
it takes a high tolerance

343
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:23,740
for adversity and uncertainty.

344
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:25,940
But stick to it,

345
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:27,460
strive to understand it

346
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:29,460
and you're going to stay out of the spiral.

347
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:30,460
Boy Scouts,

348
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:34,460
Boy Scouts,

349
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:38,460
Boy Scouts,

350
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:42,460
Boy Scouts.

351
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:51,460
Find me a letter,

352
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:53,460
send it my name.

353
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:56,460
Email that is folks.

354
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:59,460
Email that is folks.

355
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:02,460
and here's an answer to one of your emails.

356
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:12,460
So this email question came in,

357
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:14,460
I'm going to withhold the name and the location.

358
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:15,460
Here's what the writer said.

359
00:15:15,460 --> 00:15:17,460
So our troops been using a patrol method

360
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:18,460
for about a year

361
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,460
Now. I really like the concept, but my problem is

362
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:22,460
I don't agree with the hands-off policy,

363
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:25,460
meaning do not interfere with the patrols.

364
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:27,460
I've been rebuffed by our scout master

365
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:29,460
for stopping games that were getting too rough

366
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:30,460
in my opinion,

367
00:15:30,460 --> 00:15:32,460
where I've pointed out things I thought can be approved on,

368
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:35,460
only to have the scout master tell me that I'm in the wrong

369
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:37,460
Now. I've been a den leader in Cub Scouts

370
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:38,460
and a Cub master.

371
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:40,460
I just started a new Cub pack

372
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:42,460
and I'm also an assistant scout master.

373
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:45,460
I've done a lot of training, including the scout master training.

374
00:15:45,460 --> 00:15:47,460
Hands-off leadership might work

375
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:49,460
well with a group of older boys,

376
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:51,460
but I believe our younger scouts need supervision.

377
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:53,460
Our oldest scout is about 15

378
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:56,460
and the other boys are between 11 and 12..

379
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:59,460
Some of the decisions being made by these younger scouts

380
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:01,460
need to be gone over by the adult leaders.

381
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,460
Our troop meetings are very poorly planned.

382
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:05,460
I think they could spend their time much better.

383
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,460
I feel that I'm not really needed

384
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:09,460
and I don't know why I'm putting on a uniform

385
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:10,460
and showing up to these meetings

386
00:16:10,460 --> 00:16:12,460
if I'm just going to sit there and watch.

387
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:14,460
It's a waste of my time.

388
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:17,460
Am I wrong to feel that these scouts need more supervision?

389
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:19,460
I know my son is only 12

390
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:22,460
and he has sometimes has trouble making the right decision.

391
00:16:22,460 --> 00:16:24,460
Shouldn't we be much more involved with what's going on?

392
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:27,460
Well, I say that what you describe

393
00:16:27,460 --> 00:16:29,460
is really sounds to me

394
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:31,460
like somebody is applying the patrol method,

395
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:33,460
the way that it should be applied,

396
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:35,460
and it doesn't look right, does it?

397
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:37,460
It won't,

398
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:39,460
You know it won't,

399
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:41,460
Leave the scouts alone

400
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:44,460
and follow the scout master's lead for now.

401
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:46,460
It's pretty typical

402
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:49,460
that people, especially people who've been involved with Cubs,

403
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:51,460
are going to get into a scout troop

404
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:53,460
using the patrol method and using youth leadership

405
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:55,460
and they're going to have a lot of reservations

406
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:57,460
about what's going on

407
00:16:57,460 --> 00:17:00,460
and they may not understand what's going on.

408
00:17:00,460 --> 00:17:02,460
What looks like 45 minutes of playtime

409
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:04,460
may be something else,

410
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:07,460
and if it was only 45 minutes of playtime,

411
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,460
well, you have to sit back and you have to say:

412
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,460
what are our scouts doing?

413
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:14,460
How are they developing themselves individually

414
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:17,460
and their patrol as a group?

415
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:19,460
The age of the scouts matters a little bit,

416
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:22,460
but not as much as everybody may think.

417
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:25,460
Younger scouts can manage much more

418
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:27,460
than we are comfortable with letting them manage.

419
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:29,460
You know, a lot of times-

420
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:31,460
especially if you're a parent-

421
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:33,460
the younger scout trying to manage

422
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,460
buying food and cooking food

423
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:37,460
and things like that boy.

424
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:39,460
it just seems really, really sketchy

425
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:41,460
and it's a tough thing to do.

426
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:43,460
but you know what they do, fine.

427
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:45,460
They do fine.

428
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:47,460
They plan a meeting and hold a meeting

429
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:49,460
and things like that.

430
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:51,460
Of course you're going to look at that.

431
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:53,460
if a boy who's 12 years old plans a meeting,

432
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:55,460
He's not going to plan it to an adult standard,

433
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:57,460
He's going to plan it to a 12 year old boy standard,

434
00:17:57,460 --> 00:17:59,460
which means he is going to plan it

435
00:17:59,460 --> 00:18:01,460
to have the most fun

436
00:18:01,460 --> 00:18:03,460
and to efficiently get through

437
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:05,460
whatever business he needs to get through

438
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:07,460
so that they can go out and run around and play.

439
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:09,460
Of course he's going to do that.

440
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:11,460
Now you work with them.

441
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:13,460
so you work with them, of course,

442
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:15,460
but if they're getting done what they need to get done

443
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:17,460
and they're happy with it,

444
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:19,460
let's move on.

445
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:21,460
I understand you feel like you're wasting your time,

446
00:18:21,460 --> 00:18:23,460
but you and I wear a uniform to do one thing

447
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:25,460
and one thing only,

448
00:18:25,460 --> 00:18:27,460
and that's to make it possible for scouts

449
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:29,460
to do the real work of scouting

450
00:18:29,460 --> 00:18:31,460
In a scout troop. that means doing things

451
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:33,460
with some adult oversight

452
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:35,460
but independent of adult interference.

453
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:37,460
If you don't agree with the scout master's assessment

454
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:39,460
of the scout's abilities

455
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:41,460
and the way that he's administering things,

456
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:43,460
you can choose to accept that

457
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:45,460
you may be wrong

458
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:47,460
and see if you may be able to learn something

459
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:49,460
from this experience,

460
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:51,460
or you can honestly find another troop

461
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:53,460
that more closely reflects the way you want to do things.

462
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:55,460
I'm not trying to be dismissive of your concerns.

463
00:18:55,460 --> 00:18:57,460
There are plenty of troops out there

464
00:18:57,460 --> 00:18:59,460
that are run on a very efficient basis

465
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:01,460
by the adults

466
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:03,460
and then there are other troops

467
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:05,460
that are run on the patrol method by the boys.

468
00:19:05,460 --> 00:19:07,460
You're going to see a huge difference

469
00:19:07,460 --> 00:19:09,460
between the two.

470
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:11,460
if one more closely reflects

471
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:13,460
what you think scouting should be,

472
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:15,460
go to that one.

473
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,460
It's really pretty simple:

474
00:19:17,460 --> 00:19:19,460
Training. just as I said

475
00:19:19,460 --> 00:19:21,460
in scout master's ship in 7 minutes

476
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:23,460
or less just a moment ago.

477
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:25,460
training is very important

478
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:27,460
and it's an important source of knowledge,

479
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:29,460
but being trained does not mean

480
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:31,460
that you possess experience or skill.

481
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,460
Volunteering as a cub leader

482
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:35,460
is a wonderful service,

483
00:19:35,460 --> 00:19:37,460
but you have to understand that cub scouts

484
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:39,460
do things appropriate to their age level

485
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:41,460
and

486
00:19:41,460 --> 00:19:43,460
scouts do things appropriate to their age level.

487
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,460
Experience as a leader

488
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:47,460
at one level does not mean

489
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:49,460
that you know or understand

490
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:51,460
anything about what happens

491
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:53,460
at the next level.

492
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:55,460
What you might need to do is kind of shift out a cub scout gear

493
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:57,460
and work at understanding

494
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:59,460
how a scout troop really works.

495
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:01,460
You've got to have a lot of patience

496
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:03,460
and tolerance for the kind of chaos

497
00:20:03,460 --> 00:20:05,460
that this looks like.

498
00:20:05,460 --> 00:20:07,460
You have a tight schedule and you don't feel as if you're needed-

499
00:20:07,460 --> 00:20:09,460
and this may very well be true,

500
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:11,460
honestly, because scout troops need

501
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,460
fewer adults involved.

502
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:15,460
Perhaps you should concentrate on the cub pack

503
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:17,460
and share scouting with your son,

504
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:19,460
go camping every now and then

505
00:20:19,460 --> 00:20:21,460
show up at a meeting when you can.

506
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:23,460
in fact, you might found out that it's a lot less

507
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:25,460
frustrating and a better time for the both of you.

508
00:20:25,460 --> 00:20:27,460
So, honestly,

509
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,460
I'm not trying to be dismissive of

510
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:31,460
anyone's concerns about this.

511
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:33,460
I'm just trying to explain what happens

512
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:35,460
not to uncommon in troops that use the patrol method,

513
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:37,460
that parents are going to be concerned

514
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:39,460
and new volunteers are going to be concerned

515
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:41,460
over the way things happen.

516
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:43,460
My best advice is to hang on,

517
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:45,460
study and be open to learning

518
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:47,460
what's happening. Sometimes

519
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:49,460
adult volunteers are going to be oil and water

520
00:20:49,460 --> 00:20:51,460
for each other and if you don't really understand

521
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:53,460
or appreciate or agree with what's going on.

522
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,460
you may really want to think about

523
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:57,460
helping another troop. So, anyways,

